Author: RomanDeckert (Wikimedia Switzerland / Association of Swiss Archivists, International Archives Week 2020)
License: CC BY-SA 4.0
Direct: https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8c/CICR-ICRC-PublicArchives-HQ-WWII-files_RomanDeckert09062020.jpg
Used on: s01 (hero cover) — real photo of a document archive room (ICRC public
archives, Geneva): rows of shelved file boxes receding down a narrow aisle.
Directly anchors Case 1's "поиск ответа в 200 PDF юридического архива" scenario
and, more broadly, foreshadows the seminar's central question — faced with a
large body of material and a task, which architecture (and how much of one) do
you actually need? Rejected alternatives (documented for traceability):
"A choice of path" (geograph.org.uk 547628, CC BY-SA 2.0) — real fork-in-path
photo but low resolution (640x480) and the fork itself unclear at a glance;
"Colourful ladder.jpg" (Wikimedia, CC BY-SA 4.0) — turned out to be a
playground/fence structure, not legible as a ladder.
